      "writtenOn": "2025-02-17T09:06:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is only meant for `SharedTextureMemoryD3D11Texture2D` where the ID3D11Texture2D is imported into Dawn unlike `SharedTextureMemoryDXGISharedHandle`.\nThat  ID3D11Texture2D is only used by single D3D device. It makes no sense to use fences. Note: even if you deferred contexts, fences are also useless. Fences cannot be used by deferred contexts anw. Deferred contexts has to be inserted to the main context\u0027s stream. Hence Begin/EndAccess makes no sense for `SharedTextureMemoryD3D11Texture2D` and it makes it unnecessariyl complicated to book keeping the accesses.\n\nWe are planning to make small optimization for `SharedTextureMemoryD3D11Texture2D` in chrome. fine-grained Begin/EndAccess is still used for `SharedTextureMemoryDXGISharedHandle`",
      "parentUuid": "264834b4_44312220",
      "revId": "f263ec69dbf4414a971071a6efa3aeff5106f9c9",
